; Negative fixture: the schema document's names must be injective, and the guard must fail the
; CONSUMER's own json-gen run. This spec is deliberately UNBUILDABLE at the json-gen `cargo run`
; step — `integration_tests::json_schema_name_stolen_fails` asserts the run fails and names the
; check-B message.
;
; The STOLEN-NAME case, and the reason a name ledger alone is not enough: the type that claims the
; name FIRST has no registration row of its own. `alpha_parent` sorts before `shared` in the row
; order (rows come from a `BTreeMap<RustIdent, _>` per scope), so its row registers first and pulls
; `hidden_ext` in transitively; `hidden_ext` carries `@no_json_schema_export`, so it never appears in
; the ledger, and its hand-written `JsonSchema` impl claims the name `Shared`. The later `shared` row
; — whose derived `schema_name()` is also `Shared` — is then published as `Shared2`, a name decided by
; registration order rather than by this spec. Only the "did this row keep its own name?" check sees
; it.
alpha_parent = [x: hidden_ext]
hidden_ext = _CDDL_CODEGEN_EXTERN_TYPE_ ; @no_json_schema_export
shared = [y: uint]
